{"type":"npc","name":"Nimbus Dirge","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":370,"temp":0,"max":370,"details":"void healing"},"ac":{"value":39,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":30,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"fly","value":60}],"details":""},"immunities":[{"type":"death-effects","exceptions":[]},{"type":"disease","exceptions":[]},{"type":"paralyzed","exceptions":[]},{"type":"poison","exceptions":[]},{"type":"sleep","exceptions":[]}],"weaknesses":[{"type":"mental","value":10,"exceptions":[]}],"resistances":[{"type":"bludgeoning","value":10,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["common","jotun","melodian","necril","sussuran"],"details":""},"level":{"value":17},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Cloud giant musicians are renowned for their skills, particularly with the harp. Some of these musicians act as patrons and muses for members of the smaller ancestries.</p><p>Nimbus dirges are the creations of a group of legendary necromancers unwilling to lose access to their favorite performers to the icy grip of death. The necromancers murdered the cloud giants in a brutal ritual, then grafted their signature harps into their bodies where their right arms had once stood. Yet the horrific cacophonies these profane beings created were a cruel mockery of the music they once loved. Disappointed by their failure, the necromancers turned their creations loose. Most of these nimbus dirges still wander the world to this day, bringing destruction wherever they go.</p><h2>Command Performance</h2><p>While beautiful music grieves nimbus dirges, they can't stop themselves from seeking it out. Weeping, they watch a skillful musical performance, sometimes demanding encore after encore. These command performances often end in bloodshed: when a nimbus dirge is inspired to play along, or when a fatigued musician strikes a false note, the resulting discordance drives the nimbus dirge into a murderous rage.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 1,875/4,300/8,000 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning), armor (light, medium), shield, perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Athletics, Crafting, Intimidation, Lore [Music], Nature, Performance)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> air, body, bane, charisma, constitution, death, elongating, energy resistant (void), mind, mind shield, music, sensory (darkvision, scent), spells (Primal: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.qlxM7Ik3uUeUIOcv]{Canticle of Everlasting Grief}, @UUID[Compendium.battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.spells.M2uQp36xa8fzsyAZ]{Dissonance}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.O6VQC1Bs4aSYDa6R]{Mask of Terror}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.9XHmC2JgTUIQ1CCm]{Mist}), strength, sturdy, throwing, unholy, water, wild, winged</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Nathan Berg","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":9},"dex":{"mod":5},"con":{"mod":9},"int":{"mod":6},"wis":{"mod":7},"cha":{"mod":10}},"perception":{"details":"cloudsight","mod":29,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"},{"type":"scent","acuity":"imprecise","range":30}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":31,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":27,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":29,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":31},"athletics":{"base":33},"crafting":{"base":31},"intimidation":{"base":36},"nature":{"base":33},"performance":{"base":36}},"traits":{"value":["air","giant","undead","unholy"],"rarity":"rare","size":{"value":"huge"}}},"_id":"zZTxSLlG7xjk8XnV","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/nimbus-dirge.webp","prototypeToken":{"name":"Nimbus Dirge","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"width":3,"height":3,"textur